---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = "What Is Lorem Ipsum and Why Designers Use It - Toolkit Lab";
const description = "Where lorem ipsum placeholder text comes from, why designers use it, and how to use it well in mockups and layouts.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/guides/what-is-lorem-ipsum.html">
<aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>
    <div class="wrap article">
      <p class="note"><a href="/guides.html">Guides</a> / Design</p>
      <h1>What Is Lorem Ipsum and Why Designers Use It</h1>
      <p class="lead">Lorem ipsum is placeholder text that designers and printers have used for centuries. It looks like Latin, but it is not meant to be read. That is the point: it lets a layout be judged without the distraction of real words.</p>

      <h2>Where it comes from</h2>
      <p>The passage is adapted from a work by the Roman writer Cicero, first printed in the 1500s. Printers scrambled and shortened the original sentences to make a sample text. The result has a letter pattern and word length similar to ordinary English, so pages look finished.</p>

      <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>

      <h2>Why use placeholder text at all</h2>
      <p>Real copy changes often and can pull attention to itself. If a headline is a real sentence, people read it and comment on it instead of checking the spacing, font size and column width. Placeholder text keeps the discussion on the design.</p>

      <h2>Using it well</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Match the amount of text to what the final content will be, so line lengths and page height are realistic.</li>
        <li>Use it for layout reviews, not for final copy. Replace it before you publish anything.</li>
        <li>Mix paragraph lengths and include a short line, so headings and spacing get tested too.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Try it yourself</h2>
      <p>The <a href="../tools/lorem-ipsum-generator.html">Lorem Ipsum Generator</a> makes paragraphs, sentences or words, with an option to start with the familiar opening line. Copy the result in one click.</p>

      <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
    </div>
    <aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>

</Base>
